Direct Object Reference (IDOR) due to missing ownership validation",\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\n      "line_range": [20, 90],\n      "description": "Endpoints that operate on a specific todo item (GET/{id}, PUT/{id}, DELETE/{id}) do not verify that the requesting user owns the todo. If todos are user‑scoped, this allows one user to access or modify another user\'s todos.",\n      "impact": "Data leakage and unauthorized modification or deletion of other users\' todos.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Extract the user identifier from HttpContext.User (e.g., a claim) and add a where clause to ensure the todo belongs to that user before returning or modifying it.",\n      "code_before": "var todo = await dbContext.Todos.FindAsync(id);\\n\\n            return todo is null\\n                ? TypedResults.NotFound()\\n                : TypedResults.Ok(new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, todo.CreatedAt, todo.UpdatedAt));",\n      "code_after": "var userId = User.FindFirst(ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;\\n            var todo = await dbContext.Todos\\n                .FirstOrDefaultAsync(t => t.Id == id && t.UserId == userId);\\n\\n            return todo is null\\n                ? TypedResults.NotFound()\\n                : TypedResults.Ok(new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, todo.CreatedAt, todo.UpdatedAt));",\n      "references": ["OWASP A01:2021 – Broken Access Control", "CWE-639: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key"]\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-003",\n      "severity": "medium",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Missing input validation on request DTOs",\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\n      "line_range": [35, 80],\n      "description": "The CreateTodoRequest and UpdateTodoRequest parameters are not validated. Empty or malformed titles/descriptions could be persisted, leading to data integrity issues.",\n      "impact": "Invalid data may be stored, causing downstream issues or poor user experience.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Add data annotation attributes (e.g., [Required], [StringLength]) to the request DTOs, or integrate a validation library like FluentValidation and invoke validation before processing the request.",\n      "code_before": "public record CreateTodoRequest(string Title, string Description?, bool Completed);",\n      "code_after": "public record CreateTodoRequest(\\n    [Required][StringLength(200)] string Title,\\n    [StringLength(2000)] string? Description,\\n    bool Completed);",\n      "references": ["CWE-20: Improper Input Validation", "OWASP A03:2021 – Injection"]\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-004",\n      "severity": "low",\n      "category": "performance",\n      "title": "Read‑only queries lack AsNoTracking, causing unnecessary change tracking overhead",\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\n      "line_range": [20, 45],\n      "description": "GET endpoints retrieve data only for reading, yet the EF Core query tracks entities by default. This adds unnecessary overhead, especially under load.",\n      "impact": "Reduced throughput and increased memory usage for read‑heavy workloads.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Add .AsNoTracking() to the query before filtering/ordering for GET endpoints.",\n      "code_before": "var query = dbContext.Todos.AsQueryable();\\n\\n            if (completed.HasValue)\\n            {\\n                query = query.Where(t => t.Completed == completed.Value);\\n            }\\n\\n            var todos = await query\\n                .OrderBy(t => t.CreatedAt)\\n                .Select(t => new TodoResponse(t.Id, t.Title, t.Description, t.Completed, t.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt))\\n                .ToListAsync();",\n      "code_after": "var query = dbContext.Todos.AsNoTracking().AsQueryable();\\n\\n            if (completed.HasValue)\\n            {\\n                query = query.Where(t => t.Completed == completed.Value);\\n            }\\n\\n            var todos = await query\\n                .OrderBy(t => t.CreatedAt)\\n                .Select(t => new TodoResponse(t.Id, t.Title, t.Description, t.Completed, t.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt))\\n                .ToListAsync();",\n      "references": ["EF Core Performance Considerations"]\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-005",\n      "severity": "low",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Unhandled exceptions may expose internal error details",\n      "file": "src/Api/Features/Todos/TodoEndpoints.cs",\n      "line_range": [15, 100],\n      "description": "No try/catch is present around EF Core operations. Unhandled exceptions will bubble up, potentially returning detailed stack traces to clients if no global exception handling middleware is configured.",\n      "impact": "Information leakage and poor client experience; attackers may gain insight into the system.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Wrap the EF Core calls in a try/catch block and return a ProblemDetails response on failure, or rely on a global exception handler that returns generic error messages.",\n      "code_before": "using var dbContext = dbContextFactory.CreateDbContext();\\n            var todo = await dbContext.Todos.FindAsync(id);\\n\\n            return todo is null\\n                ? TypedResults.NotFound()\\n                : TypedResults.Ok(new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, t.CreatedAt, t.UpdatedAt));",\n      "code_after": "try\\n            {\\n                using var dbContext = dbContextFactory.CreateDbContext();\\n                var todo = await dbContext.Todos.FindAsync(id);\\n\\n                return todo is null\\n                    ? TypedResults.NotFound()\\n                    : TypedResults.Ok(new TodoResponse(todo.Id, todo.Title, todo.Description, todo.Completed, todo.CreatedAt, todo.UpdatedAt));\\n            }\\n            catch (Exception ex)\\n            {\\n                // Log the exception (logger injected or ILogger)\\n                return TypedResults.Problem(\\"An unexpected error occurred.\\", statusCode: StatusCodes.Status500InternalServerError);\\n            }",\n      "references": ["CWE-209: Generation of Error Message Containing Sensitive Information", "OWASP A09:2021 – Security Logging and Monitoring Failures"]\n    }\n  ],\n  "positive_observations": [\n    "Uses IDbContextFactory for proper DbContext lifecycle management",\n    "All mutating endpoints use async/await correctly",\n    "Timestamps are consistently set using DateTimeOffset.UtcNow",\n    "Partial updates in PUT use null‑coalescing to preserve existing values",\n    "CreatedAtRoute is used correctly for POST responses",\n    "Endpoints are grouped and tagged for OpenAPI/Swagger documentation",\n    "No raw SQL strings – EF Core queries are parameterized, eliminating injection risk"\n  ]\n}\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>>\n```'}